To establish orthology rigorously without small-database ascertainment bias, every candidate `tBLASTn` hit (bitscore ≥ 28 or _E_ ≤ 0.01) in all 18 _NRG1–LPL_ intervals was tested by reciprocal `BLASTx` against the entire _Alligator mississippiensis_ RefSeq proteome (48,040 proteins, `GCF_030867095.1`) both at the clustered locus-span level and at the individual top-HSP exon level (±30 bp; Table S2b). Evaluating both windows exposed an analytical pitfall: when multi-exon pseudogene spans encompass >5 kb of degraded intronic sequence (`Strcam` and `Aptrow` _AMBN_, span 5.3 kb), intronic transposable or uncharacterized hits outscore the short \~150-bp coding exon in full-span `BLASTx`, whereas top-HSP exon reciprocal `BLASTx` unequivocally confirms _Alligator_ ameloblastin as the proteome-wide best hit (`Strcam`: `XP_019346384.1`, 51.2 bits, _E_ = 9.5×10#super[−9] vs. runner-up 28.9 bits; `Aptrow`: `XP_019346385.1`, 50.8 bits, _E_ = 8.9×10#super[−9] vs. runner-up 32.7 bits).

In _Gallus gallus_ `GRCg7b` chromosome Z (`NC_052572.1`), three distinct unannotated relics preserve the exact ancestral transcriptional orientation (`−` strand) and physical order (`ENAM` Exon 8 → `ENAM` Exon 6 → `AMBN` Exon 3; @tab1, Figure 1B), with distinct, explicitly graded evidence tiers:
- *_ΨENAM_ Exon 8 (whole-proteome reciprocal `BLASTx`-confirmed):* The genomic union of the `tBLASTn` core vs. full RefSeq _Alligator_ `ENAM` (`55,155,480–55,157,125`, `−`, 1,646 bp, 40.8 bits, _E_ = 1.2×10#super[−4]) and the intra-avian `BLASTn` span vs. kakapo Exon 8 (`55,155,490–55,157,464`, `−`, 1,975 bp genomic span across 2,074 gapped alignment columns, 63.4% identity, 317 bits, _E_ = 7.3×10#super[−87]) covers `NC_052572.1:55,155,480–55,157,464` (`−`), a *1,985-bp* 1-based inclusive span (BED `55155479–55157464`). It is single-copy within the chicken _NRG1–LPL_ interval (1 hit in `dc-megablast`), and whole-proteome reciprocal `BLASTx` returns _Alligator_ enamelin (`XP_019346375.1`, 41.6 bits, _E_ = 0.004 full span; `XP_019346377.1`, 41.6 bits, _E_ = 2.7×10#super[−5] top HSP) with zero non-enamelin hits at _E_ ≤ 10 across 48,040 proteins in the full span.
- *_ΨENAM_ Exon 6 (nucleotide-, splice-, and synteny-confirmed; not `BLASTx` reciprocal-confirmed):* Recovered across `NC_052572.1:55,160,529–55,160,677` (`−`, 149-bp flanked `BLASTn` span; BED `55160528–55160677`) situated 3,064 bp strictly upstream of Exon 8 and 1,108 bp strictly downstream of the non-overlapping Ensembl lncRNA `ENSGALG00010014557` (`55,161,786–55,165,166`). The homologous coding exon core itself spans 47 bp (`NC_052572.1:55,160,570–55,160,616`, `−`, BED `55160569–55160616`, corresponding to 48-bp phase-0 _Alligator_ Exon 6, `XP_019346377.1` codons 168–183). Orthology is supported at the nucleotide and synteny levels: single-copy in `NRG1–LPL` (1 hit in both `dc-megablast` and `blastn`, 269 bits, _E_ = 4.9×10#super[−74]), direct `BLASTn` (`-word_size 7`) vs. _Alligator_ Exon 6 (±60 bp) at 72.6% identity over 135 bp (60.8 bits, _E_ = 5.3×10#super[−11] vs. runner-up 30.1 bits, _E_ = 0.089; bare 48-bp core 35.6 bits, _E_ = 4.2×10#super[−4]), intra-avian `BLASTn` vs. _A. rowi_ Exon 6 at 78.0% identity (115 bits, _E_ = 2.7×10#super[−27]), canonical `AG...GT` splice borders, and an in-frame `TAA` stop at codon 171 (`CAA→TAA`) immediately followed by a 1-nt frameshift deletion (`GGA→-GA`). Direct empirical testing confirmed that chicken _ΨENAM_ Exon 6 does *not* pass whole-proteome reciprocal `BLASTx` against 48,040 _Alligator_ proteins under standard (`-seg yes`/`-seg no`, _E_ ≤ 10; top non-specific hit `XP_019343727.1`, 28.5 bits, _E_ = 0.29) or ultra-sensitive (`-word_size 2 -evalue 1000 -comp_based_stats 0`) settings—an expected consequence of a 47-bp exon truncated at codon 4 (whereas the intact 48-bp _Alligator_ Exon 6 positive control returns `XP_019346377.1` at 37.7 bits, _E_ = 3.6×10#super[−5]\; Table S2b).
- *_ΨAMBN_ Exon 3 (whole-proteome reciprocal `BLASTx`-confirmed):* Spans `NC_052572.1:55,168,855–55,168,992` (`−`, 138 bp; BED `55168854–55168992`), single-copy (`dc-megablast`), forward `tBLASTn` 56.6 bits (_E_ = 4.0×10#super[−10], 50.0% identity over 46 aa), whole-proteome reciprocal `BLASTx` confirmed to _Alligator_ ameloblastin (`XP_019346384.1`, 45.8 bits, _E_ = 5.1×10#super[−7] top HSP vs. non-ortholog runner-up 26.6 bits), with a chicken-specific 3' splice-acceptor mutation (`AG→AC`; Section 2.5).

Beyond chicken, whole-proteome reciprocal `BLASTx` confirmed _ΨENAM_ in 7 of 8 birds (all except _Tinamus guttatus_ [`Tingut`], whose marginal 29.6-bit hit dropped to 0.00 excess under 1,000 permutations and reciprocally matched kinase `DCLK3`) and in _Chrysemys picta_ and _Chelonia mydas_ (whereas _Pelodiscus sinensis_ [`Pelsin`]'s 30.0-bit fragment dropped to 0.00 excess at 1,000 permutations, empirical _p_ = 0.061, and _Gopherus evgoodei_ [`Gopevg`]'s 29.3-bit hit failed reciprocity). Crucially, we confirmed an unannotated *_ΨAMTN_ relic on kakapo chromosome Z* (`Strhab`, `bStrHab1.2.pri`, `NC_044302.2:51,216,319–51,216,444`, `−`, 126 bp, `tBLASTn` 37.4 bits, _E_ = 2.8×10#super[−4]\; reciprocal best hit across 48,040 proteins = _Alligator_ amelotin `XP_014451634.1`, 38.1 bits, _E_ = 1.9×10#super[−4] vs. runner-up 26.9 bits) positioned in exact ancestral syntenic order downstream of _ΨENAM_ (@tab1; Figure 1A). A lower-confidence _ΨAMTN_ top-HSP candidate also occurs in exact syntenic order in mallard duck (`Anapla`, `NC_092621.1:53,220,153–53,220,311`, `+`, `tBLASTn` 34.3 bits, _E_ = 3.0×10#super[−3]\; top-HSP reciprocal `XP_014451634.1`, 35.0 bits, _E_ = 5.0×10#super[−3], though its 7.6-kb multi-HSP span is masked by an intronic hit to `LOC132245913`, 134 bits; Table S2b).

