Four auxiliary controls reinforce and delimit these Level 2 findings (Table S6):
1. *_ODAPH_ physical deletion vs. _ODAM_ uninformative negative:* Across 17 measurable sauropsids, toothed controls retain 16.8–47.8 kb between _CDKL2_ and the adjacent downstream anchor (_THAP6_/_PARM1_), housing an intact 3,784-bp _ODAPH_ gene in _Alligator_ (Figure 1C). All eight birds exhibit drastic syntenic gap collapse to 0–2,447 bp (`0 bp` in `Galgal`, `146 bp` in `Anapla`, `859–2,447 bp` in the remaining six birds), and `Pelsin` collapses to `132 bp`—physically shorter than the _Alligator_ _ODAPH_ locus and providing Level 2 evidence of physical deletion. By contrast, _ODAM_ yielded no significant hit even in toothed _Alligator_, _Anolis_, or _Python_ (best `tBLASTn` _E_ ≥ 0.21; amphibian sensitivity check on _Xenopus_ yielded _E_ = 0.042–1.6), classifying _ODAM_ absence as an uninformative Level 1 negative.
2. *Empirical `tBLASTn` blind-spot calibration (_ΨAMEL_):* The chicken _ΨAMEL_ pseudogene sequenced by #pcite(<sire2008>) (`EU340348`) maps at 100.0% nucleotide identity across four exon blocks (513 bp) to `GRCg7b` chr1 (`NC_052532.1:124,410,142–124,413,840`, `−`) between intact flanking anchors _MSL3_ (121 bits) and _MID1_ (455 bits). Yet querying this exact interval with _Alligator_ `AMELX` yields 0 HSPs under `-seg yes` and a noise-floor 25.8 bits under `-seg no`, proving that absence of `tBLASTn` signal cannot rule out a retained pseudogene relic.
3. *Independent whole-genome alignment coverage (`multiz100way`):* Across 29 human `hg38` coding exons of _ENAM_, _AMBN_, and _AMTN_, UCSC `multiz100way` independently aligns 56.4–63.0% of _ENAM_ CDS in _C. mydas_ and _C. picta_, 41.0% in _Amazona vittata_, and 64.4% of _AMBN_ CDS in two falcons (_Falco cherrug_, _F. peregrinus_); however, functional _Alligator_ (`allMis1`) yields 54 raw frameshifts against `hg38`, restricting `multiz100way` strictly to coverage-only support (Table S6).
4. *Chromosome Z recombination context:* Anchoring `GRCg7b` chicken _ΨENAM_ and _ΨAMBN_ to `galGal3` via exact 32-mer matching (4,380/4,380 and 1,893/2,650 concordant 32-mers) places both relics inside recombination bin 1784 of the #pcite(<elferink2010>) linkage map (male recombination rate 3.94 cM/Mb; _NRG1–LPL_ window weighted average 2.27 cM/Mb, 54th percentile of 122 chrZ bins vs. chrZ mean 3.00 and autosomal mean 2.97 cM/Mb) @groenen2009, rejecting a recombination cold-spot explanation for relic persistence.

#heading(level: 2, numbering: none)[2.3. Compositional, SEG-Masking, Length, and Substitution-Rate Bias in Enamel IDPs]

Sequence profiling with `segmasker` (`-window 12 -locut 2.2 -hicut 2.5`) confirms stark compositional divergence between globular flanking controls and mineralized-tissue IDPs (Figure 2A; Table S3a). Globular _LPL_ exhibits low Pro+Gln content (6.9–8.2%), high Shannon entropy (4.19–4.22 bits/aa), and 0.0% (_Anolis_) to 3.1% (_Alligator_) `SEG`-masked residues. By contrast, sauropsid enamel proteins (_ENAM_, _AMBN_, _AMTN_) contain 18.0–25.9% Pro+Gln and 46.6–57.3% disorder-promoting SCPP residues (P, Q, S, D, E, G, N), with 5.0–13.9% `SEG`-masked sequence. Functional osteogenic SCPP/SIBLING IDPs (_IBSP_, _SPP1_, _SPARCL1_)—intact across all 18 amniotes—exhibit even stronger low-complexity enrichment, reaching 25.5% (_SPP1_) and 52.8% (_IBSP_) `SEG`-masked residues in _Anolis_ (14.4% and 46.0% in _Alligator_), while the cross-chromosome negative control _DSPP_ is 47.4% `SEG`-masked.

Because a 20-permutation 95th percentile ($p_(95,"null")$) is governed by the second-largest draw and suffers high sampling variance, we executed a high-permutation sensitivity benchmark across all 18 species × 14 queries × 2 `SEG` modes (`504` cells; `N = 20, 200, 500, 1,000` global composition-preserving shuffles, seed `20261119`, plus `N = 200` local 20-aa block-preserving shuffles, seed `20261120`, and 2,000-replicate bootstrap 95% CIs, seed `20261121`; Table S3b–c). Observed bitscores reproduced `504/504` identically. Increasing permutations from `N = 20` to `N = 1,000` narrowed median bootstrap 95% CI width on $p_(95,"null")$ 3.4-fold (from `2.70 bits` to `0.80 bits`) and eliminated an extreme `N = 20` collapse on heavily `SEG`-masked `DSPP_Amis` (CI width `25.87 → 0.70 bits`). Across all 504 cells, median $|p_(95,1000) - p_(95,20)|$ was `0.86 bits` (95th percentile `2.13 bits`), flipping 12 marginal noise-floor calls (`0.26–1.42 bits`, dropping `Pelsin` and `Tingut` `ENAM_Amis` to `0.00` excess while confirming `Strhab` `ENAM_Acar` at `0.80 bits`, empirical _p_ = 0.024). Across the 14 queries, null $p_(95,1000)$ scales positively with query length (`-seg yes` Spearman $rho = +0.651$, _p_ = 0.012; `-seg no` $rho = +0.702$, _p_ = 0.005) and Shannon entropy ($rho = +0.769$, _p_ = 0.001) and negatively with `SEG`-masked fraction (`-seg yes` Pearson _r_ = −0.795, _p_ = 0.0007; `-seg no` _r_ = −0.670, _p_ = 0.009, reflecting BLAST+ composition-based score adjustment even without `SEG`).

Evaluating null-corrected retention indices ($sum "excess"("ENAM", "AMBN", "AMTN") \/ "excess"("LPL")$, `N = 1,000`, with bootstrap 95% CIs propagated across all four queries; all `LPL` denominators 119.4–256.1 bits) exposes two compounding artifacts in translated bitscore metrics (Figure 2B–C; @tab2, Table S3b–c):

First, *phylogenetic query asymmetry confounds non-equidistant scores.* Under full-length _Alligator_ queries (`-seg yes`), crocodylians score 12.73–15.61, toothed squamates—diverged \~281 Ma per TimeTree 5 @kumar2022—drop to 1.49–2.59, and edentulous _Chelonia mydas_ (`2.17`, 95% CI `2.16–2.18`) and _Chrysemys picta_ (`1.56`, 95% CI `1.56–1.57`) overlap or exceed toothed _Python bivittatus_ (`1.69`, `1.68–1.70`) and _Podarcis muralis_ (`1.49`, `1.49–1.49`; Figure 2C1). Switching to equidistant _Anolis carolinensis_ queries (\~281 Ma to Crocodylia, Testudines, and Aves) eliminates this overlap cleanly: toothed Crocodylia score `2.27–2.80` (narrowest gap CI: `2.26` vs. `0.58`), edentulous Testudines drop to `0.00–0.58`, and Aves drop to `0.00–0.12` (Figure 2C2).

Second, and more fundamentally, *functional intrinsically disordered proteins suffer steep bitscore attenuation in Aves even under purifying selection, and equal divergence time does not imply equal substitution rates.* Under equidistant _Anolis_ queries (`N = 1,000`; @tab2; Figure 2B):
- Globular *_LPL_* (`0.0%` SEG) is invariant to `-seg yes` vs. `-seg no` and scores _higher_ in Aves (median `135.6 bits`, range `133.1–143.5`, *112.6%* of Crocodylia `120.4 bits`; 20-aa block null `135.9 bits`), with median top-HSP amino-acid identity `88.7%` in Aves versus `80.0%` in Crocodylia and `73.9%` in Testudines. This directly demonstrates clade-specific rate heterogeneity despite equidistant divergence—and rules out generalized avian substitution-rate acceleration or locus-wide alignment breakdown across _NRG1–LPL_.
- Functional bone *_IBSP_* (`52.8%` SEG) drops in Aves to median `40.5 bits` (*74.5%* of Crocodylia `54.3`; 20-aa block null `42.7 bits`) under `-seg yes`. Disabling `SEG` (`-seg no`) boosts Crocodylia to `99.3 bits` while Aves rises only to `48.2 bits` (*48.5%* of Crocodylia, a *51.5%* drop; top-HSP identity `45.5%` in Aves vs. `55.4%` in Crocodylia). Under closer archosaurian _Alligator_ queries, functional avian _IBSP_ drops to `7.7–26.6 bits` excess (median `15.6`, *13.6%* of Crocodylia `114.8 bits`; Table S3c).
- Functional bone *_SPP1_* (`25.5%` SEG) drops in Aves to median `16.8 bits` (*50.0%* of Crocodylia `33.5 bits`; range *7.3–23.9 bits* under `-seg yes`; 20-aa block null `18.3 bits`), directly overlapping the excess bitscore range of decayed avian _ENAM_ (`0.0–12.7 bits`) and _AMBN_ (`0.0–15.4 bits`; Figure 2B). Similarly, intact SCPP progenitor _SPARCL1_ (`Allmis` query) drops to `74.1 bits` in Aves (`13.3%` of Crocodylia `556.1 bits`; Table S3c).

Because birds and turtles represent only _n_ = 2 independent evolutionary origins of edentulism, all clade comparisons above are reported descriptively without pooled-species inferential _p_-values @saputra2021. Together, these permutation-calibrated controls establish quantitatively that depressed `tBLASTn` bitscores in Pro/Gln- or Asp/Glu-rich IDPs cannot serve as standalone evidence of pseudogenization.

