#heading(level: 2, numbering: none)[2.4. Level 3 Splice-Aware Coding Lesions and Splice-Site Disruptions]

To separate structural pseudogenization from fast-evolving functional disorder, we aligned full-length _Alligator_ RefSeq proteins (`ENAM` `XP_019346377.1`, 1,078 aa; `AMBN` `XP_019346386.1`, 390 aa; `AMTN` `XP_014451634.1`, 328 aa; flanking positive control `LPL` `XP_019346320.1`, 477 aa) across all 18 _NRG1–LPL_ intervals with `miniprot` (v0.18-r281; Figure 3A, Table S4).

The flanking positive control *_LPL_* aligned cleanly across *18/18 species* (8,246 aligned aa total: 2,695 toothed + 5,551 edentulous) with *0 frameshifts, 0 premature stop codons (0.00 lesions/1,000 aa), and 133/133 canonical `GT-AG` introns* (0 non-canonical splice junctions), ruling out systematic `miniprot` alignment artifacts or assembly-quality confounding across the exact same genomic intervals. Similarly, toothed enamel controls (_n_ = 15 alignments spanning 9,394 aligned aa across Crocodylia and Squamata, with _Gavialis_ _AMTN_ partially truncated by its 14.8-kb scaffold contig N50) exhibited only 1 isolated `miniprot` frameshift call in _Anolis_ _AMBN_ (`fs@171` at 45.6% aa identity across \~281 Ma divergence, despite an intact native RefSeq ORF `NP_001315156.1` of 377 aa), establishing an empirical cross-clade alignment false-positive floor of *0.11 lesions/1,000 aa* (0 premature stop codons; 92/93 canonical `GT-AG` introns).

In stark contrast, edentulous enamel pseudogenes exhibited *41 frameshifts and 29 premature stop codons* (70 coding lesions across 4,122 pooled aligned aa = *16.98 lesions/1,000 aa*, or *17.49 lesions/1,000 aa* across the 7 substantial lesioned alignments spanning 4,002 aa—a *>150-fold enrichment* above the empirical toothed floor; Figure 3A):
- _Chrysemys picta_ (`Chrpic`) _ENAM_: 12 frameshifts + 4 PTCs (22.44/1,000 aa across 713 aa, 66.1% cov) — corroborating our native Gnomon audit (Table S7).
- _Strigops habroptila_ (`Strhab`) _ENAM_: 8 frameshifts + 9 PTCs (19.63/1,000 aa across 866 aa, 80.3% cov).
- _Apteryx rowi_ (`Aptrow`) _ENAM_: *7 frameshifts + 8 PTCs (19.18/1,000 aa across 782 aa, 72.5% cov) plus a disrupted `GT→AT` splice donor* spanning a 1,100-bp intron (Intron 6). Notably, using the legacy partial GenBank entry `QOX06214.1` (849 aa, missing 212 N-terminal residues) completely failed to align _A. rowi_ _ENAM_ (0% coverage; Table S4), demonstrating how query completeness governs pseudogene recovery.
- _Chelonia mydas_ (`Chemyd`) _ENAM_: 8 frameshifts + 3 PTCs (19.16/1,000 aa across 574 aa, 53.2% cov).
- _Dromaius novaehollandiae_ (`Dronov`) _AMBN_: 1 frameshift + 3 PTCs (13.94/1,000 aa across 287 aa, 73.6% cov).
- _Chrysemys picta_ (`Chrpic`) _AMBN_: 3 frameshifts + 1 PTC (10.26/1,000 aa across 390 aa, 100% cov).
- _Chelonia mydas_ (`Chemyd`) _AMBN_: *2 frameshifts + 1 PTC (7.69/1,000 aa across 390 aa, 100% cov) plus a disrupted `GT→AT` splice donor* spanning a 1,552-bp intron (Intron 8) — corroborating our native Gnomon audit (Table S7).

Because `miniprot` depends on seeded 4-mer amino-acid chains against a crocodylian query, highly degraded avian _ENAM_ loci falling below \~35% protein identity with dense frameshifts (`Galgal`, `Anapla`, `Dronov`, `Strcam`) were not spanned by `miniprot` even though intra-avian nucleotide `BLASTn` (63–89% nt identity) readily recovered 1.7–2.5 kb of orthologous Exon 8 and Exon 6 in all seven birds for Level 4 analysis below. Audit of `miniprot` intron lengths also uncovered an instructive quality-control failure mode: full-length `ENAM` initially chained an implausible 58.4-kb intron in _C. picta_ to an upstream 382-bp low-complexity hit (`NC_088796.1:129,180,576–129,180,957`), which whole-proteome reciprocal `BLASTx` proved was *protein SON* (_E_ = 0.010), not enamelin. Imposing a biological 25,000-bp maximum-intron filter segmented this distal chaining artifact cleanly without altering any genuine enamelin exon (Table S4).

#heading(level: 2, numbering: none)[2.5. Level 4 Dual-Aligner Shared Mutations, ML Ancestral Reconstruction, and Neutral PTC Incongruence]

To test which inactivating lesions reflect shared ancestry versus convergent decay or secondary reversal, we extracted verified coding exons of _Alligator_ _ENAM_ (Exons 6 and 8; complete 8-exon CDS = 3,237 bp, 100% exact translation to `XP_019346377.1`) and _AMBN_ (Exons 3, 4, and 9; complete 9-exon CDS = 1,173 bp, 100% exact translation to `XP_019346386.1`), recruited homologous avian and testudine fragments, and aligned each exon independently with *MAFFT `L-INS-i`* (v7.525) and *MUSCLE 5* (v5.3) alongside all three toothed crocodylians (`Allmis`, `Cropor`, `Gavgan`). All three crocodylian controls yielded *0 coding lesions in both aligners across every dataset* (Table S5a).

Because non-synonymous sense substitutions occurred along the \~240–250 Myr stem separating Crocodylia from crown Neornithes prior to stop-codon formation at 6 of the 16 avian _ENAM_ Exon 8 PTC sites (`codons 311, 439, 559, 601, 844, 1003`, plus a synonymous `TCA→TCG` transition at `codon 1022`), we distinguish explicitly between the *_Alligator_ reference protein coordinate/residue* (`XP_019346377.1:p.Xxx###Ter` for _ENAM_, `XP_019346386.1:p.Xxx###Ter` for _AMBN_; avoiding HGVS `c.` nucleotide prefixes) and the *reconstructed crown-avian ancestral codon and amino acid* (Table S5a). Requiring exact reference coordinate, mutation-class, and carrier-set agreement across both aligners yielded *23 robust shared coding mutations* across avian and testudine _ENAM_ and _AMBN_ (16 avian _ENAM_ Exon 8 PTCs + 1 avian _ENAM_ frameshift + 2 turtle _ENAM_ PTCs + 2 avian _AMBN_ Exon 3 PTCs + 1 avian _AMBN_ Exon 4 deletion + 1 turtle _AMBN_ Exon 4 insertion; Figure 3B–C; @tab3, Table S5a).

To avoid treating raw _Alligator_ codons as avian ancestral states or equating distinct stop triplets with independent origins a priori, we fitted constrained maximum-likelihood models (`IQ-TREE 3.1.4`, `GTR+G --ancestral`, plus 10,000-replicate RELL formal topology tests `-zb 10000 -zw -au`) @wong2026 to the avian _ENAM_ Exon 8 alignment under all three rooted Palaeognathae resolutions (Table S9): *T1* (Novaeratitae = `Aptrow` + `Dronov`, `Strcam` basal; established by independent genome-wide non-coding and retroelement phylogenomics, @sackton2019), *T2* (`Strcam` + `Dronov`), and *T3* (`Strcam` + `Aptrow`). Alongside its external phylogenomic support, _ENAM_ Exon 8 independently favors *T1* in both MAFFT ($ln L = -15","237.86$) and MUSCLE ($ln L = -15","423.30$), formally rejecting *T2* ($Delta ln L = -22.96$ in MAFFT, $-22.10$ in MUSCLE; $p_"KH" <= 0.0040$, $p_"SH" <= 0.0040$, $p_"WSH" <= 0.0045$, $c_"ELW" <= 0.0016$, $p_"AU" <= 0.0015$) and *T3* ($Delta ln L = -23.18$ and $-22.15$; $p_"KH" <= 0.0033$, $p_"SH" <= 0.0033$, $p_"WSH" <= 0.0096$, $c_"ELW" <= 0.0012$, $p_"AU" <= 0.0017$; Table S9).

Mapping all 23 consensus coding mutations and flanked-MSA exon splice borders (re-audited with ±60–80 bp intronic flanks aligned in both MAFFT and MUSCLE; Table S5b) onto *T1* while grading outgroup and sister-clade coverage establishes subclade minimum dates alongside fundamental limits on PTC dating:
1. *Palaeognathae (`Aptrow`, `Dronov`, `Strcam`):* Supported by *3 outgroup- and sister-verified congruent PTCs in _ENAM_ Exon 8* (all with Palaeognathae ML $P_"stop" >= 0.983$ and sense codons confirmed in Neognathae and Crocodylia): reference `p.Gln370Ter` (`CAA [Gln] → TGA`), reference `p.Phe601Ter` (where all three crocodylians carry `TTT` [*Phe*], crown Neornithes and Neognathae ML reconstruct `TAT` [*Tyr*, $P = 0.899$ and $0.946$; retained as `TAT` in `Galgal`/`Strhab` and `TAC` in `Anapla`], and Palaeognathae underwent the 1-step transversion `TAT [Tyr] → TAA [Ter]`, $P_"stop" = 0.994$), and reference `p.Trp751Ter` (`TGG [Trp] → TGA`). These are accompanied by a *shared 3' splice-acceptor disruption at _ENAM_ Exon 6* (`AG→AC` in `Strcam` and `Aptrow`, further mutated to `GT` in `Dronov`, while `Allmis`, `Galgal`, and `Anapla` preserve canonical `AG`), and an aligner-invariant *16-nt frameshift deletion in _AMBN_ Exon 4* (`XP_019346386.1` codon 109, `nt 113–128`, verified absent in all three crocodylians and three toothed squamates). Because standard `dc-megablast` recovered no Neognathae sequence at _AMBN_ Exon 4 (`covered_without = -` in Table S5a), and ultra-sensitive recruitment (`blastn -word_size 7` / `tblastn -word_size 2`) recovers a syntenic _AMBN_ Exon 4 relic only in `Anapla` (`57.2 bits`, _E_ = 9.3×10#super[−10], canonical `AG..GT`)—which preserves the intact ancestral length across an upstream 8-nt Palaeognathae deletion (`nt 61–76`) but carries a shorter, aligner-variable 10-nt deletion at codon 109—we classify the 16-nt deletion as an *observed shared Palaeognathae coding lesion* (`SHARED_CLADE_LESION_SISTER_UNRECOVERED`) rather than an exclusively proven crown-Palaeognathae synapomorphy.
2. *Novaeratitae (`Aptrow` + `Dronov`):* Anchored by *5 outgroup- and sister-verified congruent PTCs in _ENAM_ Exon 8* (all with `Strcam`, Neognathae, and Crocodylia retaining sense codons and Novaeratitae ML $P_"stop" >= 0.954$: `p.Gly270Ter` `GGA [Gly] → TGA`; `p.Ser401Ter` `TCC [Ser] → TGA`; reference `p.Ser559Ter`, where Crocodylia carry `AGC` [Ser], crown Neornithes and `Strcam`/Neognathae carry `TGT`/`TGC` [*Cys*, Neornithes ML $P = 0.958$], and Novaeratitae underwent `TGT [Cys] → TGA`; `p.Gln667Ter` `CAG [Gln] → TAG`; and reference `p.His844Ter`, where Crocodylia carry `CAC` [His], crown Neornithes ML reconstructs `CAA` [*Gln*, $P = 0.886$], and Novaeratitae underwent `CAA/CAG [Gln] → TGA`), *2 congruent PTCs in _AMBN_ Exon 3* (`p.Ser56Ter` `TCA→TAA`, `p.Gln62Ter` `CAA→TGA`), and a *shared 5' splice-donor disruption at _ENAM_ Exon 6 (`GT→AT`)* confirmed in both aligners and in `miniprot`.
3. *Galloanserae (`Galgal` + `Anapla`):* Anchored by *1 outgroup- and sister-verified congruent frameshift indel* in _ENAM_ Exon 8 (`XP_019346377.1` codon 619: net +2 nt relative to Crocodylia, representing a 1-nt deletion inside an ancestral avian +3-nt insertion retained in-frame in all Palaeognathae and `Strhab`) plus *1 congruent PTC* (`p.Gly558Ter` `GGA [Gly] → TGA`, Galloanserae ML $P_"stop" = 0.880$). In flanked-MSA _AMBN_ Exon 3, `Anapla`, `Aptrow`, `Dronov`, and `Strcam` all retain canonical `AG..GT` borders in both aligners, whereas `Galgal` exhibits a derived 3' splice-acceptor disruption (`AC..GT`; Table S5b).
4. *Psittacopasserae (`Strhab` + `Taegut`):* Anchored by *1 outgroup- and sister-verified congruent PTC* in _ENAM_ Exon 8 at reference coordinate `XP_019346377.1:p.Trp1003Ter` (Psittacopasserae ML $P_"stop" = 0.895$). Here, all three crocodylians carry `TGG` (*Trp*), Palaeognathae carry `GGG`/`GGC` (*Gly*), `Galgal` carries `TAC` (*Tyr*), `Anapla` is uncovered (`---`), and `Strhab` + `Taegut` share `TGA` (*Ter*). Under independent nucleotide-site `GTR+G` ML ASR, multiplying the three per-position base marginals at crown Neornithes (`T` × `G` × `C`) yields a composite argmax of `TGC` (*Cys*, $P = 0.343$) slightly ahead of `TGA` (*Ter*, $P = 0.291$) and `TGG` (*Trp*, $P = 0.168$), even though no extant bird carries `TGC` and 3-step nucleotide Fitch parsimony equally allows a direct `TGG (Trp) → TGA (Ter)` transition or an intermediate `TGC (Cys) → TGA (Ter)` transversion (Table S5a).
5. *Sampled Durocryptodira Subclade (`Chemyd` + `Chrpic`):* Supported by *1 shared 1-nt frameshift insertion in _AMBN_ Exon 4* (`XP_019346386.1` codon 123, verified absent in all three crocodylians and three toothed squamates), a *shared 3' splice-acceptor disruption in _AMBN_ Exon 4* (`AG→AC`, retaining minor canonical `GC` donor in both aligners; Table S5b), and *2 shared PTCs in _ENAM_ Exon 8* (`p.Gln753Ter` `CAG→TAG`, `p.Ala859Ter` `GCA→TGA`). Because neither _Gopherus evgoodei_ (`Gopevg`, Testudinidae, within Durocryptodira) nor basal _Pelodiscus sinensis_ (`Pelsin`, Trionychia) retains recoverable sequence across _AMBN_ Exon 4 or _ENAM_ Exon 8 codons 753/859 even under `-word_size 7` `blastn` and `-word_size 2` `tblastn`, these four lesions are classified as *shared subclade lesions of the sampled `Chemyd` + `Chrpic` lineage* (`SHARED_SUBCLADE_LESION_SISTER_UNRECOVERED`), establishing a minimum inactivation bound at the common ancestor of Chelonioidea + Testudinoidea without claiming finer phylogenetic precision across unrecovered `Gopevg`/`Pelsin` or unsampled Pleurodira.
6. *Crown Neornithes — Zero Congruent Lesions, Topology Sensitivity (`T1`–`T3`), ML ASR Dissection of Incongruent PTCs, and Coverage-Masked Neutral Simulation:* Across all 7 aligned birds, *zero coding lesions or splice disruptions were shared congruently across crown Neornithes* (Figure 3B). Under irreversible (no-reversal) parsimony on the primary topology *T1*, *6 of 16 (37.5%, nominal binomial Clopper–Pearson 95% CI 15.2–64.6%)* @clopper1934 dual-aligner shared avian _ENAM_ Exon 8 PTCs require ≥2 independent stop gains. Crucially, this proportion is topology-dependent (Table S9): under alternative Palaeognathae topologies *T2* (`Strcam` + `Dronov`) and *T3* (`Strcam` + `Aptrow`), irreversible-parsimony incongruence rises to *10/16 (62.5%, 95% CI 35.4–84.8%)* and *11/16 (68.8%, 95% CI 41.3–89.0%)*, respectively (and reversible ML ASR incongruence from *5/16 [31.2%, 11.0–58.7%]* on *T1* to *9/16 [56.2%]* on *T2* and *10/16 [62.5%]* on *T3* because the five Novaeratitae `Aptrow` + `Dronov` PTCs become non-monophyletic). Because all 16 PTCs reside within a single linked exon (_ENAM_ Exon 8), binomial confidence intervals summarize finite-site sampling uncertainty within one locus rather than independent evolutionary loci. Site-by-site ML ASR on *T1* exposes distinct mutational mechanisms (Figure 3C, Table S5a):
   - *Parallel `TGG` transition:* `p.Trp562Ter` (`TGG [Trp] → TGA` in `Strcam` + `Strhab`; Neornithes ML `TGG` $P = 0.965$, $P_"stop" = 0.031$) is a direct parallel 1-step transition.
   - *Palaeognathae CpG context with reversal ambiguity:* At reference `p.Pro311Ter` (`Dronov` + `Strcam` = `TGA`, `Aptrow` = `CGA` [Arg], Neognathae = `CAA` [Gln], _Alligator_ = `CCG` [Pro]), ML ASR reconstructs Neornithes `CAA` (*Gln*, $P = 0.542$) transitioning to a *Palaeognathae `CGA` (*Arg*) CpG codon* ($P = 0.541$) versus `TGA` (*Ter*, $P = 0.453$). Within Palaeognathae, `CGA→TGA` is a 1-step CpG transition, and ML ASR remains genuinely ambiguous between parallel `CGA→TGA` gains versus a single Palaeognathae stop followed by `TGA→CGA` reversal in `Aptrow`.
   - *Distinct stop triplets (`p.Ala439Ter`, `p.Trp615Ter`, `p.Gln684Ter`):* Because `TAA↔TAG` (codon 684) and `TAA↔TGA` (codon 615) differ by a single transition, distinct stop triplets *alone* cannot rule out a shared stop followed by stop-to-stop drift (whereas `TAG↔TGA` at reference `p.Ala439Ter`—where Neornithes ML reconstructs `TCA` [*Ser*, $P = 0.320$]—differs by 2 substitutions). Independent origins are instead supported jointly by phylogeny and ML ASR: at codon 684, ML reconstructs Neornithes `CAA` ($P = 0.548$) and Galloanserae `CAA` ($P = 0.714$) alongside Palaeognathae `TAG` ($P = 0.974$), favoring a Palaeognathae stop gain plus an independent `CAA→TAA` mutation in `Galgal`; at codon 615, `Aptrow`, `Galgal`, and `Anapla` retain `TGG` (Neornithes `TGG` $P = 0.695$), requiring ≥2–3 events across `Strcam`/`Dronov` (`TGA`) and `Strhab` (`TAA`).
   - *Codon 1022 (`p.Ser1022Ter`) — ML ASR inference versus missing sister coverage and parsimony equiparsimony:* At reference `p.Ser1022Ter`, Crocodylia carry `TCA` (*Ser*), Palaeognathae carry sense codons (`Strcam = TCG` [Ser], `Aptrow = CCG` [Pro], `Dronov = GGA` [Gly]; Neornithes ML `TCG` [*Ser*], $P = 0.652$), `Galgal` and `Strhab` carry `TAG` (*Ter*), `Taegut` carries `AAA` (*Lys*, 2 substitutions from `TAG`), and `Anapla` is *uncovered* (`---`). Under binary Fitch parsimony, two independent gains (`Galgal` + `Strhab`) and one crown-Neognathae gain followed by `TAG→AAA` reversal in `Taegut` are strictly equiparsimonious (2 steps each). Under reversible `GTR+G` ML ASR, the long passerine branch leading to `Taegut` and the missing `Anapla` state lead ML to assign high posterior probability to a crown-Neognathae `TAG` stop across all three topologies ($P_"stop" = 0.926$ on *T1*, $0.908$ on *T2*, $0.909$ on *T3*; Table S9). Because `Anapla` is uncovered and `Taegut` is sense `AAA`, we distinguish this probabilistic ML inference (`5/16 = 31.2%` incongruent if counted as a reversed Neognathae stop) from directly observed, unreversed synapomorphies (`6/16 = 37.5%` under irreversible parsimony).
   - *Coverage-masked vs. unmasked neutral stop-gain simulations (Table S8):* Auditing our neutral K80 ($kappa = 4.0$) Monte Carlo model of the 878-codon (2,634-bp) _ENAM_ Exon 8 explained why an unmasked simulation assuming 100% sequence coverage across all 7 birds (`seed 20261122`) overpredicted the absolute number of shared PTCs (median *25.0–29.0*, 95% range `16.0–39.0`, placing the `16` observed shared PTCs in the lower tail at two-sided empirical $p = 0.004"–"0.052$, even though its simulated incongruence fraction of `47.8–53.6%` overlapped `37.5%`, $p = 0.084"–"0.340$; Table S8). In the empirical `ENAM_exon8_aves` alignment, partial exon decay reduces dual-aligner per-species codon coverage to *22.7%* in `Taegut` (`199/878` codons), *58.7–60.4%* in `Anapla`/`Galgal`, and *79.0–82.5%* in Palaeognathae and `Strhab`, leaving *0 of 878 codons simultaneously covered across all 7 birds*. When the exact empirical dual-aligner per-species coverage mask and missing-taxon parsimony (`None` for uncovered tips) are applied (`seed 20261123`, 1,000 replicates per scenario across 48 parameter combinations; Table S8), baseline K80 evolution ($kappa = 4.0$, empirical branch scale $1.0 times$, $t_"stem" = 0.00"–"0.05$, reconstructed Neornithes ML root sequence) predicts a median of *16.0–19.0 shared PTCs* (95% range `10.0–27.0`; observed `16` at the `48.8th–23.4th` percentile, two-sided empirical $p = 0.538"–"1.000$), an unconditional incongruence fraction of *40.0–44.4%* (95% range `16.7–68.4%`, two-sided $p = 0.618"–"0.848$ vs. observed `37.5%`), a *conditional incongruence median of 37.5%* among replicates matching $N_"shared" = 16$ ($n = 111$ at $t_"stem" = 0.00$; `40.0–44.4%` for $N_"shared" in [14, 18]$), and a *median of 0.0 crown-Neornithes PTC synapomorphies* ($P(N_"syn" = 0) = 50.3"–"94.6\%$). Varying $kappa in {2.0, 4.0, 6.0}$, branch-length scaling ($0.65 times$ to $1.25 times$, yielding median `11.0–21.0` shared PTCs), and topologies `T1`–`T3` confirmed that incongruence rates remain high (`30.8–48.0%`) across all plausible neutral regimes (Table S8).

