// 4. MATERIALS AND METHODS
// =============================================================================
#heading(level: 1, numbering: none)[4. Materials and Methods]

#heading(level: 2, numbering: none)[4.1. Taxon Sampling, Nomenclature, and Dual-Database Annotation Audit]

Eighteen sauropsid NCBI RefSeq reference genomes (3 Crocodylia, 3 Squamata, 4 Testudines, 8 Aves) plus _Homo sapiens_ `GRCh38.p14` (`GCF_000001405.40`) were audited programmatically via the NCBI Datasets v2 REST API and `datasets` CLI (`v18.38.0`, audited `2026-11-19`; Table S1). To eliminate abbreviation ambiguity (notably between _Taeniopygia guttata_ and _Tinamus guttatus_), all species are assigned unambiguous six-letter codes in Table S0 (`Taegut`, `Tingut`, etc.). For _Gallus gallus_ `GRCg7b` (`GCF_016699485.2`), both NCBI RefSeq Annotation Release 106 (`Ggal_genomic.gff`) and Ensembl Release 116 (`Gallus_gallus.bGalGal1.mat.broiler.GRCg7b.116.gtf.gz`, SHA-256 `407e3e270da9668eecc205b685493d157abbd8fa80bc698a65bfd3ed3a5f8009`) were parsed locally. For the four edentulous RefSeq `PROTEIN_CODING` models (`Chrpic` _ENAM_, `Chemyd` _AMBN_, `Strcam` _AMELX_, `Aptrow` _AMELX_), native genomic CDS exons, intron splice dinucleotides, Gnomon modification notes, ±2-kb `N`-gaps, ±200-kb flanking synteny, and whole-proteome `BLASTp` orthology against _Alligator_ were audited directly from NCBI GenBank/GenPept records (`08_audit_protein_coding_models.py` through `08c_b2_exact_ptc_and_tableS7.py`; Table S7). Genomic coordinates follow 1-based inclusive convention throughout, with 0-based half-open BED equivalents listed in Table S2a.

#heading(level: 2, numbering: none)[4.2. Syntenic Interval Extraction and High-Permutation Compositional Controls]

For each of the 18 sauropsids, two genomic windows were retrieved via NCBI E-utilities (`efetch`): (i) the _NRG1–LPL_ enamel-cluster interval (±60 kb padding around _NRG1_ and _LPL_, or ±800 kb around the single annotated flanking gene in `Dronov` and `Tingut`; Table S2a), and (ii) the _IBSP–SPP1–SPARCL1_ osteogenic IDP control interval (±100 kb padding). Sixteen protein queries—full-length RefSeq _Alligator_ `ENAM` (`XP_019346377.1`, 1,078 aa), legacy partial GenBank `ENAM` (`QOX06214.1`, 849 aa), `AMBN` (`XP_019346386.1`, 390 aa), `AMTN` (`XP_014451634.1`, 328 aa; `KYO35092.1`, 375 aa), globular positive control `LPL` (`XP_019346320.1`, 477 aa), cross-chromosome negative control `DSPP` (`XP_059578269.1`, 783 aa), _Alligator_ `IBSP`/`SPP1`/`SPARCL1`, and equidistant _Anolis carolinensis_ `ENAM` (`XP_062825318.1`), `AMBN` (`NP_001315156.1`), `AMTN` (`NP_001315157.1`), `LPL` (`XP_062827593.1`), `IBSP` (`XP_003221343.2`), and `SPP1` (`XP_003221344.2`)—were profiled for amino-acid composition, Shannon entropy, and low-complexity fraction using NCBI `segmasker` `v1.0.0` (`-window 12 -locut 2.2 -hicut 2.5`; Table S3a).

Baseline 20-permutation shuffles used `numpy.random.default_rng(20261017)` (`01_audit_and_fetch.py`). In the v1.0.1 statistical sensitivity benchmark (`09_permutation_sensitivity.py`), 1,000 global composition-preserving permutations per query (`default_rng(20261119)`, evaluated at nested `N = 20, 200, 500, 1,000`) plus 200 local 20-aa block-preserving permutations (`default_rng(20261120)`) were searched across all 18 enamel and 18 IDP intervals using NCBI `BLAST+` `tblastn` `v2.17.0+` @camacho2009 under both `-seg yes` and `-seg no` (`-evalue 10 -max_target_seqs 50`, identical to `02_run_alignments_wsl.sh`). Excess bitscore was defined as $max(0, "obs" - p_(95,"null"))$, empirical one-sided _p_-values as $(1 + \#{"shuf" >= "obs"}) / (N + 1)$, and 95% confidence intervals on $p_(95,"null")$ and _LPL_-normalized retention indices were estimated via 2,000 bootstrap resamples (`default_rng(20261121)`; Table S3b–c).

#heading(level: 2, numbering: none)[4.3. Whole-Proteome Reciprocal BLASTx and Single-Copy Verification]

The full _Alligator mississippiensis_ RefSeq proteome (`GCF_030867095.1`, 48,040 proteins) was formatted with `makeblastdb` (`v2.17.0+`). Every candidate enamel hit (bitscore ≥ 28 or _E_ ≤ 0.01) in `tblastn -seg yes` was extracted as (i) clustered same-strand HSPs within 15 kb (±100 bp padding) and (ii) the single highest-scoring HSP exon (±30 bp padding) and queried with `blastx` `v2.17.0+` (`-evalue 10 -seg yes -max_target_seqs 25`; Table S2b). Chicken _ΨENAM_ Exon 6 (`149-bp` `BLASTn` span, `47-bp` exon core, `±30 bp`, `±100 bp`, plus intact 48-bp _Alligator_ Exon 6 positive control) was tested additionally under `-seg yes`, `-seg no`, and `-word_size 2 -evalue 1000 -comp_based_stats 0` (`07_audit_phaseA_B1_B3.py`). Single-copy specificity within the chicken _NRG1–LPL_ interval was tested via `blastn -task dc-megablast` and `-task blastn` (`-evalue 1e-3 -dust yes`).

#heading(level: 2, numbering: none)[4.4. Level 3 Splice-Aware Alignment, Level 4 Dual-Aligner Consensus, and ML ASR]

Splice-aware protein-to-genome alignments were executed with `miniprot` `v0.18-r281` @li2023 (`-j 2 -k 4 -M 0 -n 1 -l 4 --outc=0.01 --outs=0.5`) across all 18 _NRG1–LPL_ intervals, parsing frameshifts, in-frame PTCs, and splice dinucleotides directly from PAF `cs`/`cg` strings and filtering introns >25,000 bp (Table S4).

For Level 4 shared-mutation dating, verified coding exons of _Alligator_ _ENAM_ (Exons 6, 8) and _AMBN_ (Exons 3, 4, 9) were used to recruit orthologous fragments via `blastn`, and each dataset (including all 3 toothed crocodylians as 0-lesion controls) was aligned independently with *MAFFT `v7.525`* (`--localpair --maxiterate 1000`) @katoh2013 and *MUSCLE `v5.3`* (`-align`) @edgar2022. Frameshift indels (outside ≥4-nt homopolymers and terminal 3-nt overhangs) and in-frame PTCs were retained only when identically called in both aligners. Splice borders (Table S5b) were audited exclusively from flanked intronic MSAs (±60–80 bp around verified _Alligator_ GFF3 exon boundaries, excluding terminal Exon 9 which lacks a 5' donor), and _AMBN_ Exon 4 outgroup/sister-clade coverage was further tested across all 18 _NRG1–LPL_ intervals via ultra-sensitive `blastn -word_size 7 -evalue 10 -dust no` and `tblastn -word_size 2 -evalue 50 -seg no -comp_based_stats 0` (`12_audit_v102_variants_phylo_sim.py`). Maximum-likelihood ancestral state reconstruction and formal Palaeognathae topology tests (`T1`/`T2`/`T3`; KH, SH, wKH, wSH, ELW, and AU tests with 10,000 RELL bootstrap replicates, `-zb 10000 -zw -au`) were executed in *IQ-TREE 3 `v3.1.4`* (`-m GTR+G --ancestral`) @wong2026 alongside exact Fitch parsimony, nominal Clopper–Pearson 95% CIs @clopper1934, and 1,000-replicate neutral K80 stop-gain Monte Carlo simulations evaluated across unmasked (878-codon), MAFFT-masked, and dual-aligner empirical coverage masks, $kappa in {2.0, 4.0, 6.0}$, branch-length scales $0.65 times$ to $1.25 times$, stem lengths $t_"stem" in {0.00, 0.02, 0.05}$, and topologies `T1`–`T3` (`default_rng(20261122)` in `10_audit_mutations_and_asr.py`; `default_rng(20261123)` in `12_audit_v102_variants_phylo_sim.py`; Table S5a–b, Table S8, Table S9). Auxiliary _ODAPH_/_ODAM_ gaps, UCSC `multiz100way` coverage @blanchette2004, `EU340348` _ΨAMEL_ calibration, and `galGal3` 32-mer recombination liftOver @elferink2010 are consolidated in Table S6.

#heading(level: 2, numbering: none)[4.5. Provenance, Reproducibility, and Automated Acceptance Testing]

All bioinformatics binaries ran under WSL2 (`Ubuntu-26.04`, Pixi-managed environments) orchestrated from Python 3.11 (`uv` environment), with tool versions (`tool_versions.txt`), parameters, and SHA-256 hashes logged in `runs/enamel_relics/provenance_run.jsonl`, `runs/enamel_relics/v101/provenance_*.jsonl`, `runs/enamel_relics/v102/provenance_v102.jsonl`, and `MANIFEST_SHA256.tsv`. Figures 1–3 are generated directly from `supplementary/Table_S*.tsv` using `matplotlib` (Okabe-Ito palette). An automated `pytest` suite (`tests/test_enamel_relics_audit.py`) verifies SHA-256 hashes, coordinate/indexing invariants, species/sequence counts, Level 3 lesion rates, 133/133 _LPL_ introns, Level 4 reference-vs.-ancestral codon translations, outgroup coverage tiers, `T1`–`T3` parsimony/ML sensitivity, coverage-masked K80 simulation consistency, citation integrity, PDF–Typst–Markdown synchronization, and preservation of historical release tags.

